const CONCEPTS=[
 ['Proposal','The request for insurance before it becomes a policy. Gets a Proposal No. on first Save. Moves through Quote, Underwriting, Fac Out, Bound, Prepayment, then Issued or Declined.','in'],
 ['Policy','The issued contract. Gets an official Policy No. only on Issue. From then on, every change is an endorsement.','in'],
 ['Period of insurance (POI)','The dates the cover runs: Effective Date 00:00:00 to Expiry Date 23:59:59, typically one year.',''],
 ['Sum insured (SI)','The maximum the insurer pays for a coverage. Drives premium, underwriting level and reinsurance.',''],
 ['Premium layers','Annual (formula) premium → gross premium (× POI rate) → before-VAT premium (after discount, loading or manual adjustment) → due premium (+ GST and taxes).',''],
 ['Underwriting (UW)','Risk review by an underwriter when a rule is triggered. Levels 1 and 2 route the case to different pools.','int'],
 ['Bound','Underwriting is approved and terms are fixed. All data is read-only. The case waits for Issue or Send to BCP.','int'],
 ['Prepayment (cash before cover)','Premium must be collected in BCP before the policy is issued. Easy PA auto-issues when BCP confirms collection.','int'],
 ['Endorsement','A change to an issued policy. Gets number {PolicyNo}-{Seq}, for example POTBTI01229187-001. Can create additional premium, a refund or nothing.','out'],
 ['Pro-rata (pro-rate)','Premium change in proportion to the days left: unexpired days ÷ POI days.','out'],
 ['Short-rate','A penalty refund: the customer gets only X% (e.g. 80%) of the pro-rata refund when they cancel without replacement.','out'],
 ['Cancellation','An endorsement that ends cover early, from inception (full refund) or mid-term (unearned premium refund). Policy status becomes Cancelled.','cancel'],
 ['Endorsement Undo','Rolls back the last issued endorsement (last in, first out). No new premium is calculated; the old values return.','cancel'],
 ['Renewal','A new proposal copied from the expiring policy with dates moved one year forward. Follows the new business flow.','in'],
 ['Facultative (Fac Out)','Reinsurance placed for one risk on its own, usually because the sum insured exceeds treaty capacity. The case waits in Fac Out for the XRI response.','int'],
 ['Treaty allocation','Automatic sharing of each policy with reinsurers under a treaty. Easy PA calls XRI at underwriting, bind and issue.','int']
];
